custom password hashing; disabled token validation; hardcoded signing keys;
authorization only in the frontend; Application depending on `HttpContext`;
`401` for an authenticated-but-forbidden user or `403` for missing
authentication; logged tokens; scattered role/permission magic strings;
Identity, JWT issuance, or OIDC infrastructure added without an actual need.

```csharp
// BAD — password in logs
logger.LogInformation("Login: {Email} with password {Password}", email, password);

// GOOD — non-sensitive technical identifier
logger.LogInformation(
    "Login completed for user {UserId}",
    userId);
```

Do not automatically treat as safe: secrets in `appsettings.Development.json`;
sensitive values logged only at Debug level; client-side route guards; hidden
UI buttons; CORS configuration used as a substitute for authorization.

